      "hints": [
        "Since $0 \\le \\sin^2 2x \\le 1$, $f(x)$ ranges from $q$ to $p + q$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the extrema of $f(x) = p\\sin^2 2x + q$ over $[0, \\pi]$ (since $0 \\le \\sin^2 2x \\le 1$ and $p, q > 0$):\n$$\\text{Minimum value} = p(0) + q = q$$\n$$\\text{Maximum value} = p(1) + q = p + q$$\n$$\\text{Range of } f: \\quad q \\le f(x) \\le p + q \\quad (\\text{or } [q, p + q])$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
